WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.210
Power [Recurring visual gag - anytime the
word POWER is mentioned, we should show the

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:02.210
character Power].

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:03.210
That’s why you clicked on the video.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:06.900
The answer to why you should watch Chainsaw
Man is Power.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.220
But other than this anime’s best girl - fight
me Makina fans - and the subject of next year’s

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.955
most popular Comic-Con cosplay, there are
a ton of reasons [very rapid sseries of cuts]

00:00:14.955 --> 00:00:20.310
to check out the biggest premiere this season
and there are some on this list, especially

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:26.019
the last one, that you’re not gonna believe.

00:00:26.019 --> 00:00:31.349
Everybody’s been sharing still frames from
the trailers and foaming from the mouth out

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:33.600
of pure anticipation.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.590
And now it’s finally here.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:42.110
So what exactly is all THIS?

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:51.249
Well, Chainsaw Man is adapted from a manga
by Tatsuki Fujimoto, also known for some more

00:00:51.249 --> 00:00:56.920
niche, but nontheless fantastic stories like
Fire Punch, Look Back, and Goodbye Eri.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:00.050
In theory, it’s your typical Shonen.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.230
But really only in theory.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:06.890
Here’s the premise of the story: Denji is
a teenage boy rendered homeless after inheriting

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.899
his father’s Yakuza debts.

00:01:08.899 --> 00:01:15.360
He lives in a world populated by what the
show calls devils, creatures created from

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:20.420
human fears, whose strength and power depend
on…well pretty much how much people piss

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.300
their pants because of those fears.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:29.390
After being ki-…uhm put to rest by one of
these devils, Denji’s life is saved by the

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:34.409
mandatory cute mascot, Pochita, a little chainsaw
doggo.

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:35.470
How does that work?

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:42.240
Well, Pochita becomes Denji’s heart, thus
granting him the power to fuse with the Chainsaw

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.090
Devil, and as a result becoming Chainsaw Man.

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:52.259
By far, and this is just my personal opinon,
which is right, the most badass looking anime

00:01:52.259 --> 00:01:55.000
protagonist i have ever seen.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.479
By pulling the cord that now emerges from
his chest, Denji can now activate his Chainsaw

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:02.610
Man transformation.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:03.610
Chainsaws come out of his arms.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:05.450
[blood spash animation] Chainsaws come out
of his legs.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.240
[more blood spash animation] A chainsaw comes
out of his face.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.040
[even more blood spash animation] I’m a
sick fuck for enjoying this, but hey, so are

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.330
you, so-we’re good.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:19.690
With this newfound power, Denji becomes a
Public Safety Devil Hunter: What is that you

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:20.690
ask?

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:24.690
Well it basically means, that he’s joining
a team of *clears throat* ‘good’ people

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:28.400
that keeps the world safe from the threat
of devils.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.060
Now at first glance you might say that this
is a premise that’s not too far distant

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:37.490
from the likes of Bleach, Yu Yu Hakusho, or
Jujutsu Kaisen, where irresponsible adults

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:43.590
who are too lazy or incompetent to take care
of things themselves find unwitting kids gaining

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:48.490
supernatural powers that they use to protect
humanity from evil entities.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:54.180
But whereas those shows fit the basic mold
of their Shonen Jump peers, even while having

00:02:54.180 --> 00:03:00.470
a darker edge than even more mainstream shows
like Naruto or One Piece, Chainsaw Man assuredly

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.780
does not.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:07.010
In reality, Chainsaw Man is anything but a
typical shonen.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:15.370
The biggest selling point of CSM is the super
unique tone and feel of the story.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:22.650
The chainsaws in question are not of the lumberjack
variety, but have more of a Texas Massacre

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:23.650
vibe going for them.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:27.850
In case you’re not sure, that’s code for
fucked up.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.290
This series is violent.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.120
This series is bloody.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.390
This series is gory.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:37.400
It’s dark and twisted and messed up.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:42.280
If that sort of thing appeals to you, then
Chainsaw Man might just be the show for you.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:47.520
Fujimoto’s artwork has a way of bringing
the intense action of this series completely

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.340
to life even in a static black and white image.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:56.570
I mean just looking at some of his panels
you can see the violent intensity of saws

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:59.090
ripping through flesh and bone.&nbsp;

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:02.320
And you now you don’t have squeeze your
eyes to imagine, but can actually sit on your

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:07.850
couch, eat your popcorn and watch those epic
bloody sequences and panels come to live in

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:12.290
color and motion, - where you can listen to
the roar of the chainsaws and the gushing

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.900
fountains of blood, you sick sick fu- [cut
away]

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.169
Is this the most violent manga?

00:04:18.169 --> 00:04:20.449
Of course not, Berserk exists.

00:04:20.449 --> 00:04:24.840
But if you’re into the dark, the gritty,
and the gruesome, then this is something new

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:25.840
for your repertoire.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:30.650
It’s certainly not the only show with a
dark and violent aesthetic, but to read something

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:37.159
like Chainsaw Man in the pages of Shonen Jump
alongside One Piece and My Hero Academia can

00:04:37.159 --> 00:04:40.090
come as quite a shock to some people.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:45.759
With MAPPA at the helm of the adaptation,
fans have plenty to be excited about.

00:04:45.759 --> 00:04:51.770
The studio has already proved itself capable
of some great action animation with the final

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:56.960
season of Attack on Titan and the brilliantly
rendered Jujutsu Kaisen series.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:02.259
And in addition to the action, MAPPA has experience
in more tender, emotional storytelling, being

00:05:02.259 --> 00:05:05.370
the studio that brought us Yuri on Ice.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:10.580
And speaking of that tender, emotional storytelling
- A-HA, I’ve tricked you all.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:15.259
The biggest selling point of this manga isn’t
the gritty violence at all!&nbsp;

00:05:15.259 --> 00:05:16.759
One of the most POWER-ful [reminder: Recurring
visual gag - anytime the word POWER is mentioned,

00:05:16.759 --> 00:05:21.020
we should show the character Power] assets
that Chainsaw Man has is its world building.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:26.580
It starts with that simple premise, but what
seems standard and procedural at first becomes

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:32.710
a web of political intrigue, conflicting character
motivations, and deepening mysteries.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:34.770
Hmmm…where have I heard that before?

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:35.770
[Insert One Piece footage]

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.639
Again, it starts off similar to a show such
as Bleach or Yu Yu Hakusho.

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:44.699
In the former, Ichigo Kurosaki finds newfound
powers as a Shinigami and uses them to dispatch

00:05:44.699 --> 00:05:45.699
Hollows.

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:51.699
In Yu Yu Hakusho, Yusuke Urameshi finds himself
as a spirit detective hunting rogue demons.

00:05:51.699 --> 00:05:57.580
However, both of these shows quickly abandon
their early premises in favor of a more battle-heavy

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:58.580
format.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:03.620
Bleach trades it for the tried and true formula
of fighting a new set of cool guys each arc

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:08.749
and Yu Yu Hakusho features perhaps the greatest
tournament arc of all time.

00:06:08.749 --> 00:06:16.250
And while these series are legendary among
Shonen anime, Chainsaw Man opts for a different

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:17.330
approach.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:20.879
It doesn’t skimp on the violence, obviously.

00:06:20.879 --> 00:06:23.960
This is the most blood you’re going to see
this season.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:30.689
However, beneath that tide of bombastic action
is an undercurrent of genuine philosophical

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:35.090
exploration on a level you don’t see in
many series.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:37.650
Chainsaw Man takes place in a world of devils.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:43.289
And while these devils fill a definite Monster
of the Week role, they’re also so much more.

00:06:43.289 --> 00:06:46.110
These monsters are fear manifested.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:52.620
Their strength correlates to how much cumulative
fear the human population has of the concept

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.620
which they represent.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:07:02.370
Therefore, things like the Shark Devil or
Spider Devil are fairly strong - many people

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:04.229
are scared of these concepts.

00:07:04.229 --> 00:07:09.080
In this way, the general premise is similar
to Jujutsu Kaisen, where curses are also borne

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:12.460
of fear and negative energies.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:19.590
However, Chainsaw Man tends to imbue their
devils with a greater level of social commentary

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:22.439
than JJK’s cursed spirits.

00:07:22.439 --> 00:07:26.639
This is not a dig at JJK - I still love you,
Jogo.

00:07:26.639 --> 00:07:28.689
You’re the bestest personified volcano around.

00:07:28.689 --> 00:07:33.150
But sharks and spiders are just the tip of
the ice berg.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:38.449
Chainsaw Man’s devils explore much deeper,
existential fears and that’s where things

00:07:38.449 --> 00:07:40.219
get crazy.

00:07:40.219 --> 00:07:47.240
It’s no mistake that a central antagonist
of Chainsaw Man is the Gun Devil - an unspeakable

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:51.639
monster borne out of humanity’s collective
fear of gun violence.

00:07:51.639 --> 00:07:56.430
It’s no surprise that this series has resonated
strongly with an American audience.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:08:02.169
It’s a country plagued by gun violence at
rates higher than any other developed nation.

00:08:02.169 --> 00:08:07.379
The Gun Devil and the looming threat it represents
is all too real.

00:08:07.379 --> 00:08:11.550
Chainsaw Man uses its devil premise not only
to set up awesome gruesome action, but to

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:14.930
make real political and philosophical statements.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:21.509
And Fujimoto takes his characters to hell
and back - literally - to explore the depths

00:08:21.509 --> 00:08:23.250
of human fear.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:29.279
This is a no spoiler zone, but just you wait
for the Darkness Devil to be animated.

00:08:29.279 --> 00:08:34.820
Let’s just say I’m looking forward to
seeing one of the wildest panels in all of

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:39.229
manga in motion (and I know that sounds like
hyperbole, but if you know, you know).

00:08:39.229 --> 00:08:46.160
When CSM tackles fears fundamental to the
human experience, things get absolutely bonkers.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:52.070
Yeah, lots of the abilities come from conventional
weaponry (like chainsaws) but some devils

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:55.950
have some insane POWERS on display.

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:59.620
But wait a minute,
this is like still the beginning of the story.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:02.220
Like, you see how much
longer is left in this video.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:04.000
Like, this isn't the story.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.880
What's crazy about Chainsaw man, is what comes
next.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.880
Because despite all the epic action and the
crazy powers,

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:16.360
this is nothing compared to chainsaw man’s
biggest selling point.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.950
Becuase this is where the
story gets very juicy.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:25.510
After mentoining POWER about 269 times already,
I know you didn’t come here for me to not

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:28.300
talk about Chainsaw Man’s characters.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.860
They rock.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:31.570
Every single one.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:34.080
Every cast member of Chainsaw Man is my best
friend.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.200
Denji is my best friend.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:36.490
Aki is my best friend.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:37.490
Power is best girl.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:39.260
Makima is my actual mom.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.510
Pochita is not Denji’s heart.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.020
Pochita is MY heart.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:48.570
The characters in Chainsaw Man are fully realized.

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:53.490
Each is lovable, but they’re also flawed,
corrupt, and corruptible.

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:58.310
Fujimoto clearly went to the Shrek school
of character design, because much like an

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:01.510
ogre - or an onion - these characters have
layers.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:02.730
Let’s start with Denji.

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:07.740
He’s your typical teenage boy - a homeless
debt slave to mobsters.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:13.310
Okay, this show has some definite commentary
on capitalism, wealth inequality, etc.

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:18.330
Maybe he’s not your typical teenage boy,
but in a lot of ways he’s a more realistic

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.820
teenage boy than a lot of other shonen protagonists.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:24.470
Luffy wants to be the pirate king.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.980
Naruto wants to be hokage.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:28.780
Midoriya wants to be a great superhero.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:36.310
Denji wants to get a girlfriend and - more
importantly to him - he wants to touch boobs.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:40.310
Which sounds more like the teenage boys in
your life?

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:45.200
Denji is a kid who’s never had a normal
life - he’s never had steady meals, gone

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:49.120
to school, had friends, held a real job, or
anything.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:56.280
As a result, his personality is brash, rude,
and immature - but he’s not without a level

00:10:56.280 --> 00:11:00.870
of empathy, and a willingness to play the
hero and save lives.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:06.690
As much as Chainsaw Man is about being a hero,
it’s about trying to find a purpose and

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:08.630
a role to play in one’s life.

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.340
It’s about holding down a job.

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:14.880
There’s a good reason that his transformation
into Chainsaw Man maintains a button-down

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.790
shirt and a tie.

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:19.140
He’s not wearing a superhero’s cape.

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:24.730
This form, even with a chainsaw exploding
from his face, is his workplace attire.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:31.470
Denji wants a normal life and violently slaying
devils is the only way to achieve that goal.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:35.650
Makima - another fan favorite character, because
let’s face it, they’re all fan favorite

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:41.450
characters - is the one who coerces Denji
into becoming a Public Safety Devil Hunter.

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:46.810
It’s either work for her and be treated
as a human, or hunted as a devil.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:51.850
Denji, for one, is more than happy to become
a contributing member of society and get three

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.420
square meals a day.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:57.500
It doesn’t hurt, either, that she tempts
him with the promise of a potential relationship

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:01.350
and he jumps at the chance to achieve his
dream of dreams.

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:06.590
As a leader of the Devil Hunters, Makima is
as powerful as she is mysterious and has always

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:08.720
has a way of getting what she wants.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:14.180
Aki is the edgy character of our main trio
because every series needs a Sasuke.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:19.470
However, Megumi Fushiguro of Jujutsu Kaisen
is a more apt comparison, given that Aki,

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:22.600
too, summons beasts to do some of the fighting
for him.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:27.850
Aki has made contracts with devils who will
lend their power in exchange for a price.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:32.470
For instance, he can summon the Fox Devil
for the low-low price of letting the devil

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:34.330
consume a part of his body.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:35.860
Truly a steal.

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:39.510
Aki as a character is motivated wholly by
revenge.

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:43.600
He has a personal stake in the fight against
the Gun Devil.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.210
His entire family was killed by this monster
the last time it appeared.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:52.920
As a result, he takes his job as a Devil Hunter
deadly seriously and can’t stand other characters

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:55.360
- like Denji - who don’t.

00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:58.410
Many characters - human and devil alike - are
morally grey.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:04.030
Aki and other Devil Hunters (as well as governments
and other organizations) regularly make contracts

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:05.670
with devils.

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:10.430
Devils are not a united front of evil - just
like humans, they are mostly looking out for

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:14.950
their own self-interest, and if that means
working alongside humans, then so be it.

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:20.250
Of course, there are also plenty of human
characters who demonstrate that in many ways,

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:23.390
humans can be just as vile as devils.

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:29.450
Oh, and before I forget…there’s one central
character I still haven’t talked about much…POWER.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:33.890
Power is a Blood Fiend, a fiend being a devil
that’s possessed a human corpse.

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:39.520
Power is childish, greedy, a compulsive liar,
rude, unkempt, and unsanitary.

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:45.860
She’s also taken 1st and 3rd place in the
two Chainsaw Man popularity polls and for

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:46.860
good reason.

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:51.550
As the blood devil, she can manipulate her
own and others’ blood, shaping it into various

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:57.170
weaponry - often a scythe. Power is the only
character who can match Denji’s extreme

00:13:57.170 --> 00:14:00.840
immaturity, much to the dismay of the orderly
Aki.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.820
Other than comic relief, what is her appeal,
though?

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:09.320
Well, be sure to watch the anime for all the
spoilery content that deepens her character-

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:13.670
but for now suffice to say that she loves
her cat very much, and loving a cat is easily

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:18.740
enough to redeem any other negative personality
traits.

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:23.380
Chainsaw Man has the typical shonen structure,
but it’s subversive on every level.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:28.630
It has extreme violence and gore, but still
maintains a real emotional resonance.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:35.140
It’s absurd and comical, but explores deep
philosophical topics with expert precision.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:41.690
Oh, and all of the characters are hot - which
makes Chainsaw Man the show you have to watch

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:43.550
this season.

